---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ContactSection from '../../components/ContactSection.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="How Much Does a Website Cost in Scotland in 2026? | Bastian Studio" description="Typical UK website prices in 2026, what changes the price and what you’ll pay each month, explained in plain English.">
<section id="top" class="hero-pad" style="position: relative; padding: 80px 0 88px; background: radial-gradient(900px 460px at 80% 0%, rgba(62,143,208,.22), transparent 70%), #0A1020">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="mono" style="margin: 0 0 20px; color: #9FD3F5"><a href="/" style="color: #9AA8BC; text-decoration: none">Home</a> / <a href="/guides" style="color: #9AA8BC; text-decoration: none">Guides</a> / Website cost</p>
    <h1 style="margin: 0; font-size: clamp(40px, 5.4vw, 76px); font-weight: 500; line-height: 1; letter-spacing: -.045em; max-width: 18ch">How much does a website cost in Scotland <span class="serif" style="color: #9FD3F5">in 2026?</span></h1>
    <p style="margin: 24px 0 32px; font-size: clamp(17px, 1.5vw, 20px); line-height: 1.55; color: #B7C3D4; max-width: 54ch">Typical prices, what changes them and what you’ll pay each month, explained in plain English.</p>
    <ul style="list-style: none; margin: 32px 0 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px 26px; font-size: 15px; color: #C9D4E3"><li style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="#9FD3F5" stroke-width="1.8" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7"></path></svg>6 min read</li><li style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="#9FD3F5" stroke-width="1.8" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7"></path></svg>Updated October 2026</li><li style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="#9FD3F5" stroke-width="1.8" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 8.5l3 3 7-7"></path></svg>By Sebastian</li></ul>
  </div>
</section>

<article class="sec" style="padding: 56px 0 112px">
  <div class="wrap"><div style="max-width: 720px">
    <p style="margin: 0 0 20px; font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.7; color: #C9D4E3">If you’re a small business owner in Glasgow or anywhere in Scotland, you’ve probably seen website prices from a few pounds a month to £10,000+. Here’s what you actually get at each level, and what to watch out for.</p><h2 style="margin: 48px 0 16px; font-size: clamp(26px, 2.6vw, 34px); font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -.03em; line-height: 1.15">The short answer</h2><p style="margin: 0 0 20px; font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.7; color: #C9D4E3">For most small businesses, a professionally built website from a freelancer costs <strong style="color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: 600">£800–£3,000</strong>, and agencies typically charge £3,000–£12,000. Where you land depends on the number of pages, the design, who writes the words and any extra features like online booking or a shop.</p><div class="table-like" style="margin: 8px 0 28px; border-radius: 18px; overflow: hidden; border: 1px solid rgba(159,211,245,.16)"><div class="cost-row" style="border-top: 0"><div style="font-weight: 500">DIY builder</div><div style="font-weight: 600; color: #9FD3F5">£200–£400 / year</div><div style="color: #9AA8BC">Plus your time</div></div><div class="cost-row" style="border-top: 1px solid rgba(159,211,245,.12)"><div style="font-weight: 500">One-page website</div><div style="font-weight: 600; color: #9FD3F5">£500–£1,200</div><div style="color: #9AA8BC">Single scrolling page</div></div><div class="cost-row" style="border-top: 1px solid rgba(159,211,245,.12)"><div style="font-weight: 500">Up to 5 pages</div><div style="font-weight: 600; color: #9FD3F5">£800–£3,000</div><div style="color: #9AA8BC">Freelancer, small business site</div></div><div class="cost-row" style="border-top: 1px solid rgba(159,211,245,.12)"><div style="font-weight: 500">Larger / agency</div><div style="font-weight: 600; color: #9FD3F5">£3,000–£12,000</div><div style="color: #9AA8BC">More pages, bespoke features</div></div><div class="cost-row" style="border-top: 1px solid rgba(159,211,245,.12)"><div style="font-weight: 500">Online shop</div><div style="font-weight: 600; color: #9FD3F5">£2,000–£10,000+</div><div style="color: #9AA8BC">Products, payments, delivery</div></div></div><p style="margin: 0 0 20px; font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.7; color: #C9D4E3">These are typical UK prices in 2026, from freelancers at the lower end to agencies at the top. Every project is different. For reference, my own websites start from £495 for one page and £1,195 for up to 5 pages.</p><h2 style="margin: 48px 0 16px; font-size: clamp(26px, 2.6vw, 34px); font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -.03em; line-height: 1.15">What makes the price go up?</h2><ul class="factors" style="grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr))"><li style="padding: 18px 0; border-top: 1px solid rgba(159,211,245,.16); display: grid; grid-template-columns: 26px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 10px"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="#9FD3F5" stroke-width="1.8" aria-hidden="true" style="margin-top: 2px"><path d="M4 10.5l4 4 8-9"></path></svg><span><strong style="display: block; font-weight: 500; font-size: 17px; margin-bottom: 4px">More pages</strong><span style="color: #9AA8BC; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.5">Each service, treatment or location page needs design and writing.</span></span></li><li style="padding: 18px 0; border-top: 1px solid rgba(159,211,245,.16); display: grid; grid-template-columns: 26px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 10px"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="#9FD3F5" stroke-width="1.8" aria-hidden="true" style="margin-top: 2px"><path d="M4 10.5l4 4 8-9"></path></svg><span><strong style="display: block; font-weight: 500; font-size: 17px; margin-bottom: 4px">Custom design</strong><span style="color: #9AA8BC; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.5">Bespoke design costs more than a template, and stands out more.</span></span></li><li style="padding: 18px 0; border-top: 1px solid rgba(159,211,245,.16); display: grid; grid-template-columns: 26px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 10px"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="#9FD3F5" stroke-width="1.8" aria-hidden="true" style="margin-top: 2px"><path d="M4 10.5l4 4 8-9"></path></svg><span><strong style="display: block; font-weight: 500; font-size: 17px; margin-bottom: 4px">Copywriting</strong><span style="color: #9AA8BC; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.5">Words that sell take time to get right.</span></span></li><li style="padding: 18px 0; border-top: 1px solid rgba(159,211,245,.16); display: grid; grid-template-columns: 26px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 10px"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="#9FD3F5" stroke-width="1.8" aria-hidden="true" style="margin-top: 2px"><path d="M4 10.5l4 4 8-9"></path></svg><span><strong style="display: block; font-weight: 500; font-size: 17px; margin-bottom: 4px">Features</strong><span style="color: #9AA8BC; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.5">Booking, quote forms, payments and integrations.</span></span></li></ul><h2 style="margin: 48px 0 16px; font-size: clamp(26px, 2.6vw, 34px); font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -.03em; line-height: 1.15">Monthly costs to budget for</h2><p style="margin: 0 0 20px; font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.7; color: #C9D4E3">Good news: very little. The only must-have is domain &amp; hosting, often from around £20 a year for a simple site. Maintenance, ongoing SEO and Google Ads are optional extras you can add later if and when they make sense for your business.</p><h2 style="margin: 48px 0 16px; font-size: clamp(26px, 2.6vw, 34px); font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -.03em; line-height: 1.15">Is DIY cheaper?</h2><p style="margin: 0 0 20px; font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.7; color: #C9D4E3">On paper, yes. But once you count the evenings spent learning a website builder, the slower site and the enquiries you might miss, a professional website often costs less over two or three years, and it starts paying for itself sooner.</p><h2 style="margin: 48px 0 16px; font-size: clamp(26px, 2.6vw, 34px); font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -.03em; line-height: 1.15">My advice</h2><p style="margin: 0 0 20px; font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.7; color: #C9D4E3">Start with what you need now (usually a clear, fast website with a few strong pages) and add SEO, ads or automation as you grow. And always get a fixed price in writing.</p><div class="boxpad" style="margin-top: 40px; border-radius: 24px; padding: 32px; background: linear-gradient(160deg, #14203D, #0F1830); border: 1px solid rgba(159,211,245,.2)">
      <p style="margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 24px; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -.02em">Want a price for your website?</p>
      <p style="margin: 0 0 20px; color: #B7C3D4">Tell me what you need and I’ll send a fixed quote. Free, no obligation.</p>
      <div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px"><a href="#contact" class="btn btn-ice">Get a free quote</a><a href="/prices" class="btn btn-ghost">See full price guide</a></div>
    </div>
  </div></div>
</article>

<ContactSection />

</BaseLayout>
